    {
      "id": "date",
      "title": "Date",
      "summary": "What Date does with the catalog's tasks, compared with UTV.",
      "subject": [
        {
          "path": "docs/.dev/requirements.json",
          "entityId": "example-scenario-catalog"
        }
      ],
      "criteria": [
        "Date.UTC rolls 30 February over to 2 March and month index 12 into the next year, agrees with UTV on 29 February, holds 13 September 275760 as its last time value and NaN after it, and reads negative years.",
        "Date.parse reads an ISO date as midnight UTC, rolls 30 February over, cannot tell Z from +00:00, and keeps only the instant of an offset.",
        "The constructor keeps three fractional digits, and reads local fields in the host's zone (the one test that depends on the host, on purpose).",
        "Date.now survives the trip through UTV (reads the clock on purpose; the result does not depend on the time read).",
        "getUTCDay numbers Sunday 0; setUTCMonth rolls 31 January + 1 month over to 3 March; setUTCHours carries; getTime differences are day counts or milliseconds; a round trip through UTV keeps the time value; < orders Dates; toISOString writes a time of day with a date."
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
